<title>USA: U.S. stocks higher at opening, blue chips strong.</title>
<headline>U.S. stocks higher at opening, blue chips strong.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. stocks opened higher on Tuesday, aided by strength in Treasuries and receding fears of the Democrats taking control of the House of Representatives in the U.S. elections.</p>
<p>Dow industrials were up 20 at 6062 points. The NASDAQ Index was  up four at 1224.</p>
